redumper-rgui (729-2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Add aarch64 (arm64) support: the linux-arm64 upstream binary travels as a
    Debtransform-Files extra and debian/rules swaps it in on arm64 builds
    (Architecture is now amd64 arm64). Ships UNTESTED on arm64 -- no hardware
    drive-access proof; the repackage path is architecture-neutral.

 -- gmipf <gmipf64@gmail.com>  Sat, 18 Jul 2026 01:20:00 +0000

redumper-rgui (729-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Initial package. Pinned-build compatibility package carrying upstream
    redumper b729 as /usr/bin/redumper-rgui, for consumers coupled to that exact
    build. redumper-gui is the first: its upstream bundles b729 and states that
    other versions may not be supported, and it invokes redumper as a sibling of
    its own executable -- which a distribution cannot honour by shipping a
    second /usr/bin/redumper.
  * This package was missing from the PPA, and redumper-gui Depends on it. The
    consequence was not a warning anywhere: redumper-gui uploaded, built and
    published on resolute, and was simply not installable -- measured with
    `apt-get install -s redumper-gui` in a clean 26.04 container, which answers
    "Depends: redumper-rgui but none of the choices are installable: [no choices]".
    Launchpad builds a source package against the archive but never asks whether
    the result can be INSTALLED from it, so a missing runtime dependency stays
    green all the way through.
  * Co-installable with the rolling redumper package: the build number is in the
    binary name, so no files overlap. No manpage on purpose -- the rolling
    package carries redumper(1); this is a compatibility build.

 -- gmipf <gmipf64@gmail.com>  Mon, 13 Jul 2026 21:45:00 +0200
